    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Etowah comes from a Cherokee settlement in Georgia and is traced to a Muscogee word meaning town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etowah%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1911, Etowah supported two general stores, a blacksmith, and a cotton oil mill for its seventy-five residents.",
